Subject: [PATCH 105/144] GreatDANE: harden no_legacy_deep_sign_check.py and
 wire it into the selftests (round 4, L-a)

- Flags every --deep that is not part of a --verify command. Shell commands are split on ; && || | with line
  continuations joined first. Also caught: wrapper variables ($CS --deep), deep-flag variables (DEEP=--deep,
  $DEEP, ${deep_flag}), and verify plus sign on one line.
- Python is checked through ast: implicit and '+' string concatenation are folded, and a statement with
  --verify is allowed. Comparisons ("--deep" not in line) and docstrings are not treated as commands.
- Flags legacy script names outside greatdane/tools/:
  - sign-only.sh via $G, an absolute or relative path, or a bare call;
  - build-universal.sh;
  - notarize.sh or notarize.next*.sh without --submit-existing.
  A bare "sign-only.sh" is accepted only as an os.path.join part after "tools".
- YAML: deep: true/yes/on, including quoted keys and flow style. PyYAML is used if installed, with a line parser
  otherwise; YAML string values get the shell rules.
- Scope: all text files under greatdane/, including greatdane/tests and non-.sh/.py files (Markdown fenced code
  blocks only), plus taskcluster/config.yml. Binary files are skipped.
- A trailing "nolegacy: <reason>" comment waives one line, and waived lines are always printed. There is one
  waiver, a must-not-match regex in sign_dane_macos_selftest.py.
- sign_dane_macos_selftest.py adds L0 (the guard passes on this tree), L1-L19 (each bad form is flagged),
  L20 (allowed forms pass) and L21 (a waiver is listed). Fixture text uses runtime placeholders, so the guard
  does not flag its own tests.
- --root DIR lets the selftest point the guard at fixture trees.
